# System Specifications & Execution Environment

## Host & Runtime
- **OS:** Windows native (x64) — no Linux, no WSL, no POSIX shell emulation.
- **Shell:** PowerShell 7 (`pwsh`) — no `bash`, `sh`, or `cmd.exe`.
- **Paths:** Windows backslash `\` or forward slash `/` (supported in .NET/Git). Never use Unix root paths (e.g., `/c/...`).
- **Toolchain:** .NET 10 SDK / C# 14. Solution: `SqlToAi.slnx`.

## CLI Tooling & Search
- **Search (`rg`):** Ripgrep (`rg`) is installed and available. **NEVER use `grep`** (non-native/absent).
  - Use `rg "<pattern>"` for command-line file searches.
  - When available, prefer agent workspace tools (`grep_search`, `find_symbol`); use `rg` for CLI commands.
- **No Unix Builtins:** Do not execute `ls`, `cat`, `touch`, `grep`, `find`, `sed`, `awk`, or `rm -rf`. Use PowerShell cmdlets (`Get-ChildItem`, `Remove-Item`, `Test-Path`) or agent workspace tools (`view_file`, `write_to_file`, etc.).
- **Git Paging:** Always execute Git commands with `--no-pager` (e.g., `git --no-pager diff`, `git --no-pager log`). Never trigger interactive pagers (`less`, `more`).

## Build & Test Commands
```powershell
dotnet build SqlToAi.slnx          # Compile solution (TreatWarningsAsErrors enabled)
dotnet test SqlToAi.slnx           # Run xUnit v3 test suite
```
